{"rule":"CL04","kind":"melting point","deciding":true,"level":"comparable","lo":null,"hi":165,"limit":{"lo":null,"hi":165}},{"rule":"CV05","kind":"demote-to-ceiling","deciding":true,"level":"comparable","lo":null,"hi":92,"measurementId":"V007762","value":88}],"elongationXY":[{"rule":"CV11","kind":"floor","deciding":false,"level":"set-apart","lo":3.3,"hi":null,"measurementId":"V007760","value":3.3}]},"price":null,"notes":[{"topic":"Application","items":[{"id":"Q05425","text":"Nanovia PP CF V-Slot real connectors after limonene submesion","source":"R-NANOVIA-COVERAGE-20261001-bb1289b8f753","at":"p. 1: PP-CF connector figure caption","domain":"Application","type":"Published observation","category":"application","conditions":"Own pictured exact Nanovia PP-CF connector exposure caption; no performance result, immersion time, concentration, temperature, geometry or retained strength inferred. Not a chemical-service or functional-load qualification."}]},{"topic":"Good for","items":[{"id":"Q04337","text":"Thanks to polypropylene’s close to zero water absorption rate, high chemical resistance, low density, and a native UV, Nanovia PP CF is ideal for light components exposed to the elements which require a high dimensional stability such as nautical equipment and mechanical automotive parts.","source":"R-NANOVIA-PP-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04338","text":"Polypropylene is a semi-rigid material, with high wear and shock resistance, notably used for hinges and components that endure regular flexing.","source":"R-NANOVIA-PP-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04339","text":"Humidity proof, it’s perfectly suited for both outdoor and high stress industral applications.","source":"R-NANOVIA-PP-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Benefits","items":[{"id":"Q04341","text":"The carbon fiber composition of Nanovia PP CF limit this phenomenon allowing it to be used for parts that require dimensional control in hot and humid environments.","source":"R-NANOVIA-PP-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Pitfalls and limitations","items":[{"id":"Q04342","text":"Much like polyamide (nylon), polypropylene gradually becomes more flexible with higher temperatures.","source":"R-NANOVIA-PP-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05505","text":"The product is not approved for medical applications.","source":"R-NANOVIA-PRIORITY-20261002-7672b9b52cb5","at":"p. 2: Section7.2 safe storage/use exclusion","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement","conditions":"Own SDS exclusion. No clinical/implant suitability inferred from application marketing, processing advice or another product."}]},{"topic":"Nozzle wear","items":[{"id":"Q04343","text":"A reinforced nozzle, suitable for abrasive materials is recommended.","source":"R-NANOVIA-PP-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Printing advice","items":[{"id":"Q04344","text":"In the case of bed adhesion issues, it’s recommended to either use a “raft” or a polypropylene bed.","source":"R-NANOVIA-PP-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04345","text":"The latter can be achieved by applying polypropylene film/tape to the printer bed.","source":"R-NANOVIA-PP-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04346","text":"In order for the film/tape to not unstick, a lower bed temperature is recommended.","source":"R-NANOVIA-PP-CF","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]},{"id":"G083-05","name":"LEHVOSS LUVOCOM 3F PP CF 9928 BK","maker":"LEHVOSS","variant":null,"diameter":"1.75 mm","twins":[],"composition":"with carbon fibers, black (p. 1, as the sheet states it)","certifications":null,"availab